# Chat and PTT Interface Requirements (Non-Negotiable)

## Standardized chat interface

- The **standardized chat interface** must support **single-click** switching between three layout modes: **floating** (card), **fixed** (sidebar), and **fullscreen**.
- One control (e.g. a header button) must cycle: floating → fixed → fullscreen → floating. No removal of this behavior.

## PTT (Push-To-Talk)

- **PTT** must be integrated: hold to record, release to transcribe and send.
- The voice view must show: **Secure PTT Mode**, **Transcription Preview**, and a **Hold to Record** button (or equivalent).
- Voice and text views must be switchable (e.g. "Text Concierge" / "Voice Concierge" in a menu or tabs).

## Customer-facing entry points

- Customer-facing website UI must provide:
  - **Voice Concierge** entry (opens chat in voice/PTT view).
  - **Chat Concierge** entry (opens chat in text view).
  - A floating FAB or equivalent to open the chat panel.
- The chat panel header must show **agent name + role** (e.g. "Ava CONCIERGE"), not a generic label only.
- A menu (e.g. hamburger) must allow switching Text Concierge / Voice Concierge and accessing Admin when applicable.

## Do not

- Do not remove or replace the layout cycle (floating/fixed/fullscreen) with a single fixed layout.
- Do not replace PTT with a different voice UX (e.g. always-on listening) without explicit product approval.
- Do not ship a customer chat that lacks either text or voice/PTT entry and the standardized panel.

See [docs/mvp/CHAT_AND_PTT_REQUIREMENTS.md](../../docs/mvp/CHAT_AND_PTT_REQUIREMENTS.md) for the full spec.
